.TH ADSMTR 1 "2026-06-30" "adsmt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
adsmtr \- lu\-kb\-successor runtime and REPL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adsmtr
[\fB\-\-asp\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-mode\fR \fIz3\fR|\fIfull\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adsmtr
is the interactive
.I runtime
half of the lu\-kb\-successor CLI trichotomy
.RB ( lu\-smt (1)
is the SMT\-LIB driver;
.BR adsmtc (1)
is the batch compiler). With a
.I FILE
(or a piped stdin) it solves the whole program once; with neither it
opens a read\-eval\-print loop.

Two paradigms are available:
.TP
.B lu\-kb successor
(default) \(em the unified solve, printing the
.BR UnifiedVerdict .
.TP
.B typed\-ASP
.RB ( \-\-asp ,
or
.B :asp
in the REPL) \(em the closed\-world stable\-model face. In
.B full
output mode it surfaces the 3\-valued well\-founded model: the
.IR true ", " false ", and " undefined
atoms (the experimental observation surface the AFT adoption added).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-asp
Start in the typed\-ASP paradigm.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-mode \fIz3\fR | \fIfull\fR
Select the verdict presentation.
.B z3
(the default) collapses to
.RB ( sat ", " unsat ", " unknown );
.B full
un\-collapses to the 5\-level SMT precision lattice or the 3\-valued ASP
well\-founded model.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH REPL COMMANDS
When no
.I FILE
is given, lines are accumulated into the program buffer except:
.TP
.B :check
Solve the accumulated program.
.TP
.B :reset
Clear the program buffer.
.TP
.BR :asp " / " :lukb
Switch paradigm.
.TP
.BR :full " / " :z3
Switch output mode.
.TP
.BR :quit " (or EOF)
Exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Mirrors
.BR adsmtc (1):
.B 1
=
.B unsat
(verified),
.B 0
=
.B sat
(counterexample),
.B 2
=
.BR unknown ,
.B 3
= usage / I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lu\-smt (1),
.BR adsmtc (1)
.SH AUTHOR
NEWSNIPER.
